  "title": "High-Risk Double-Consonant Trap Words",
  "intro": "Double consonants are the single largest source of lost marks in IELTS Listening gap-fill tasks. Watch closely for words with two sets of doubled letters—such as accommodation (cc, mm), committee (mm, tt, ee), embarrassment (rr, ss), and millennium (ll, nn)—versus words where a tempting double is actually single, such as professor (single f, double s) and necessary (single c, double s). (Source: IDP IELTS Difficult Words) Page 2 of 14 IELTS Listening Spelling Study Guide (1,000+ Words • 5+ Letters)",
