  "n": 3,
  "title": "Vowel Schwa & Suffix Confusion (-ance/-ence, -ant/-ent, -able/-ible)",
  "intro": "Because unstressed vowels reduce to a neutral 'uh' sound in English, pronunciation will not tell you whether to write -ance or -ence, or -able or -ible. Memorize high-frequency IELTS nouns like maintenance, independence, existence, perseverance, significance, and convenience, and remember that 'separate' has an 'a' in the middle (sep-A-rate) while 'definite' has only 'i's (def-I-nite). (Source: IELTS Listening High-Risk Spelling List)",
